1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,113
My town has 412 houses.

2
00:00:02,193 --> 00:00:04,713
And at midnight, every single one has a light on.

3
00:00:04,793 --> 00:00:06,447
Not because we're scared of the dark.

4
00:00:06,527 --> 00:00:07,980
Because of what delivers the mail.

5
00:00:08,060 --> 00:00:09,480
We moved in on a Tuesday.

6
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:11,080
Me, my little brother Theo...

7
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:13,147
...and Biscuit, the world's worst guard dog.

8
00:00:13,227 --> 00:00:15,613
Our neighbor, Mr. Pell, didn't say hello.

9
00:00:15,693 --> 00:00:17,447
He just pointed at our windows...

10
00:00:17,527 --> 00:00:19,713
...and said, 'Keep one on. Always.'

11
00:00:19,793 --> 00:00:21,847
Theo laughed. Theo laughs at everything.

12
00:00:21,927 --> 00:00:25,080
That night, I found the town rules taped inside our mailbox.

13
00:00:25,160 --> 00:00:27,213
Rule one: keep a light on at midnight.

14
00:00:27,293 --> 00:00:29,580
Rule two: never open a letter with no stamp.

15
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:30,813
Rule three... was torn off.

16
00:00:30,893 --> 00:00:32,280
11:58 PM.

17
00:00:32,360 --> 00:00:34,113
Theo hates sleeping with the light on.

18
00:00:34,193 --> 00:00:35,713
So he did the dumbest thing ever.

19
00:00:35,793 --> 00:00:36,331
Click.

20
00:00:37,393 --> 00:00:38,747
Biscuit started growling.

21
00:00:38,827 --> 00:00:39,947
Biscuit never growls.

22
00:00:40,027 --> 00:00:40,939
Twelve o'clock.

23
00:00:41,127 --> 00:00:42,580
Something slid under the door.

24
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:43,847
A letter. No stamp.

25
00:00:43,927 --> 00:00:45,313
Theo opened it anyway.

26
00:00:45,393 --> 00:00:46,847
It said: Your light is off.

27
00:00:46,927 --> 00:00:48,180
Come out and see ours.

28
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:49,647
Then I heard the window creak.

29
00:00:49,727 --> 00:00:50,880
I ran to his room.

30
00:00:50,960 --> 00:00:52,047
His bed was empty.

31
00:00:52,127 --> 00:00:55,013
And outside, a tall man with a mail sack was walking away...

32
00:00:55,093 --> 00:00:56,413
...holding Theo's hand.

33
00:00:56,493 --> 00:00:59,213
I screamed. Mr. Pell was already at our door.

34
00:00:59,293 --> 00:01:01,280
Don't chase him. Turn your light back on.

35
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:02,380
I slammed the switch.

36
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:04,213
Every light in Hollow Creek flickered.

37
00:01:04,293 --> 00:01:05,447
And the footsteps... stopped.

38
00:01:05,527 --> 00:01:07,380
In the morning, Theo was back in bed.

39
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,847
He doesn't remember anything.

40
00:01:08,927 --> 00:01:10,780
But Biscuit won't go near him anymore.

41
00:01:10,860 --> 00:01:12,780
And every night, at 11:59...

42
00:01:12,860 --> 00:01:14,684
...he asks me to turn off the lamp.

43
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:17,180
Last night, I found the rest of rule three.

44
00:01:17,260 --> 00:01:19,009
If they come back... they're not yours.

45
00:01:19,193 --> 00:01:20,239
Keep your light on.

